@@ -0,0 +1,220 @@
+/* ================================================================
+   Eatswada dynamic-pricing customer UI — additive styles.
+   Loaded LAST on the pages that use it, so it only ever adds new
+   classes (.u99-badge-*, .ew-fd-*, .ew-quote-*, .ew-bill-*) and never
+   restyles an existing rule. Design tokens come from eatswada-theme.css.
+   ================================================================ */
+
+/* ── Sponsored / Featured badges on restaurant cards ─────────────── */
+.u99-badge{
+  display:inline-flex;
+  align-items:center;
+  margin-left:6px;
+  padding:1px 6px;
+  border-radius:5px;
+  font-size:9.5px;
+  font-weight:800;
+  letter-spacing:.4px;
+  text-transform:uppercase;
+  line-height:1.5;
+  vertical-align:middle;
+  white-space:nowrap;
+}
+.u99-badge-sponsored{
+  color:#7A4A00;
+  background:#FFF0D1;
+  border:1px solid #F2CE85;
+}
+.u99-badge-featured{
+  color:#8A1F53;
+  background:#FFE7F1;
+  border:1px solid #F6B7D4;
+}
+
+/* ── Free-delivery progress on restaurant cards ──────────────────── */
+.u99-free-row.is-unlocked{ color:#1E8A5B; }
+.u99-free-row.is-unlocked .u99-free-icon svg path[style]{ fill:#1E8A5B; }
+
+/* ── Menu page free-delivery banner ──────────────────────────────── */
+.ew-fd-banner{
+  display:flex;
+  align-items:center;
+  gap:8px;
+  margin:0 0 12px;
+  padding:9px 12px;
+  border-radius:12px;
+  background:#F1F7F3;
+  border:1px solid #CFE7DA;
+  color:#1E5B41;
+  font-size:13px;
+  font-weight:650;
+  line-height:1.3;
+}
+.ew-fd-banner.is-unlocked{ background:#E7F6EE; border-color:#A9DFC3; color:#15653F; }
+.ew-fd-banner .ew-fd-banner__bar{
+  position:relative;
+  flex:1 1 auto;
+  height:6px;
+  border-radius:999px;
+  background:#DCE7E1;
+  overflow:hidden;
+  min-width:60px;
+}
+.ew-fd-banner .ew-fd-banner__fill{
+  position:absolute;
+  inset:0 auto 0 0;
+  width:0;
+  border-radius:999px;
+  background:#2C9A6A;
+  transition:width .3s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);
+}
+.ew-fd-banner .ew-fd-banner__text{ flex:0 1 auto; }
+.ew-fd-banner.is-unlocked .ew-fd-banner__bar{ display:none; }
+@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
+  .ew-fd-banner .ew-fd-banner__fill{ transition:none; }
+}
+
+/* ── Cart / checkout quote area ──────────────────────────────────── */
+.ew-quote-block{ margin-top:10px; }
+.ew-quote-note{
+  display:flex;
+  align-items:center;
+  gap:6px;
+  font-size:12px;
+  color:#6B7280;
+  margin-top:6px;
+}
+.ew-quote-expiry{
+  display:flex;
+  align-items:center;
+  justify-content:space-between;
+  gap:8px;
+  margin-top:8px;
+  padding:8px 10px;
+  border-radius:10px;
+  background:#FFF7E8;
+  border:1px solid #F3DFB4;
+  color:#7A5A12;
+  font-size:12.5px;
+  font-weight:600;
+}
+.ew-quote-expiry.is-expiring{ background:#FDECEC; border-color:#F2BEBE; color:#9B2C2C; }
+.ew-quote-expiry button{
+  border:0; background:transparent; color:inherit; font:inherit; font-weight:800;
+  text-decoration:underline; cursor:pointer; padding:0;
+}
+
+/* Decision banners (repricing / not-serviceable) */
+.ew-decision{
+  margin-top:10px;
+  padding:11px 12px;
+  border-radius:12px;
+  font-size:13px;
+  line-height:1.4;
+}
+.ew-decision__title{ font-weight:800; margin-bottom:3px; }
+.ew-decision--repricing{ background:#FFF4E5; border:1px solid #F2CE85; color:#7A4A00; }
+.ew-decision--blocked{ background:#FDECEC; border:1px solid #F2BEBE; color:#9B2C2C; }
+.ew-decision__changes{ margin:7px 0 0; padding-left:16px; }
+.ew-decision__changes li{ margin:2px 0; }
+.ew-decision__change-from{ text-decoration:line-through; opacity:.7; margin-right:4px; }
+.ew-decision button.ew-decision__action{
+  margin-top:8px;
+  padding:7px 12px;
+  border-radius:9px;
+  border:1px solid currentColor;
+  background:transparent;
+  color:inherit;
+  font:inherit;
+  font-weight:750;
+  cursor:pointer;
+}
+
+/* Bill rows (additive; the page keeps its own container) */
+.ew-bill-row{
+  display:flex;
+  align-items:baseline;
+  justify-content:space-between;
+  gap:12px;
+  padding:3px 0;
+}
+.ew-bill-row__label{ color:#4B5563; }
+.ew-bill-row__label .ew-bill-row__note{ display:block; font-size:11px; color:#8A94A6; font-weight:500; }
+.ew-bill-row--discount .ew-bill-row__value{ color:#1E8A5B; }
+.ew-bill-row--total{
+  margin-top:6px;
+  padding-top:8px;
+  border-top:1px dashed #D7DCE3;
+  font-weight:800;
+}
+
+/* ── 99-store product grid additions (additive classes only) ─────── */
+.u99-product-free{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#1E8A5B;margin-top:3px}
+.u99-add-btn.u99-add-unavailable{
+  width:auto;min-width:64px;padding:0 10px;border-radius:12px;
+  font-size:11px;font-weight:800;opacity:.7;cursor:not-allowed;
+}
+
+/* ── Category page card additions (additive classes only) ────────── */
+.res-free{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:#1E8A5B;margin:4px 0 0}
+.res-closed{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:#9B2C2C;margin:4px 0 0}
+.res-card.is-closed{opacity:.62;filter:saturate(.6);cursor:not-allowed}
+.res-card.is-closed:active{transform:none}
+
+/* Fee label helper */
+.ew-fee-label{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:5px; }
+.ew-fee-label__info{
+  width:15px; height:15px; border-radius:50%;
+  border:1px solid currentColor; opacity:.55;
+  display:inline-grid; place-items:center;
+  font-size:10px; font-weight:800; line-height:1;
+}
+
+/* ── Cart quote bill (Phase 3; additive) ─────────────────────────── */
+.ew-quote-bill{ margin:2px 0 4px; }
+.ew-qb-row{
+  display:flex; align-items:baseline; justify-content:space-between;
+  gap:12px; padding:4px 0; font-size:13.5px;
+}
+.ew-qb-row .ew-qb-label{ color:#4B5563; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }
+.ew-qb-row .ew-qb-note{ font-size:11px; color:#8A94A6; font-weight:500; }
+.ew-qb-row .ew-qb-val{ font-weight:600; color:#1F2430; white-space:nowrap; }
+.ew-qb-row--discount .ew-qb-val{ color:#1E8A5B; }
+.ew-qb-row--total{
+  margin-top:6px; padding-top:9px; border-top:1px dashed #D7DCE3; font-weight:800;
+}
+.ew-qb-row--total .ew-qb-val{ font-weight:800; }
+
+/* While a live backend quote is shown, hide the client-computed preview rows
+   so the itemized bill comes from the backend only. */
+#ct-bill.ew-quote-active .ct-bill-rows{ display:none; }
+
+.ew-qb-countdown{
+  font-size:11.5px; font-weight:600; color:#8A94A6;
+  margin:6px 0 2px; text-align:right;
+}
+.ew-qb-blocked, .ew-qb-reprice{
+  display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:flex-start;
+  background:#FFF6F6; border:1px solid #F3C6C6; border-radius:12px;
+  padding:11px 12px; margin:0 0 10px;
+}
+.ew-qb-reprice{ background:#FFFBF0; border-color:#F0DFB0; }
+.ew-qb-blocked-ic{
+  flex:0 0 auto; width:20px; height:20px; border-radius:50%;
+  background:#D64545; color:#fff; font-weight:800; font-size:12px;
+  display:grid; place-items:center; margin-top:1px;
+}
+.ew-qb-blocked-copy{ display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:3px; }
+.ew-qb-blocked-copy strong{ font-size:13.5px; color:#8E2B2B; }
+.ew-qb-blocked-copy span{ font-size:12.5px; color:#5B6472; line-height:1.45; }
+.ew-qb-selfdel{ color:#1E8A5B !important; font-weight:600; }
+.ew-qb-reprice{ flex-direction:column; gap:6px; }
+.ew-qb-reprice strong{ font-size:13.5px; color:#8A6D1B; }
+.ew-qb-reprice span{ font-size:12.5px; color:#5B6472; line-height:1.45; }
+.ew-qb-diff{ margin:2px 0 0; padding-left:16px; font-size:12.5px; color:#4B5563; }
+.ew-qb-confirm{
+  align-self:flex-start; margin-top:4px;
+  background:#1F2430; color:#fff; border:0; border-radius:10px;
+  padding:9px 14px; font-size:13px; font-weight:700; cursor:pointer;
+}
+.ew-qb-confirm:active{ transform:scale(.98); }
diff --git a/docs/rebuild/API_CONTRACTS.md b/docs/rebuild/API_CONTRACTS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cea9d6b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/rebuild/API_CONTRACTS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,260 @@
+# API Contracts — from the NEW backend (`kignas/Eatswada-`)
+
+Source of truth: backend clone at `/workspace/backend-ref`, commit `2139abb`, mounted (per
+`server.js`) at **both** `/api` and `/api/v1`. Every entry below cites the backend file it came from.
+Nothing here is guessed; where the backend is silent it is recorded as a gap in `BACKEND_GAPS.md`.
+
+Base URL used by the frontend: `https://api.eatswada.com/api` (`config.js`).
+
+Auth: `protect` middleware → `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>` (`middleware/authMiddleware.js`).
+
+---
+
+## A. Dynamic pricing & profitability
+
+### A1. `POST /pricing/quote` — `routes/pricingRoutes.js`, `controllers/pricingController.js`
+- **Auth:** `protect` (customer). **Rate limit:** 120/min.
+- **Body:**
+  ```json
+  { "restaurantId": "<24hex>", "addressId": "<24hex|null>", "items": [ { "menuItem": "<24hex>", "quantity": 2 } ], "paymentMethod": "upi|cod", "couponCode": "optional" }
+  ```
+  - `restaurantId` required (MongoId); `items` min 1 (each needs a valid menu id + qty 1..99);
+    `paymentMethod` optional `upi|cod` (default upi).
+  - Prices are **resolved server-side** from the menu — the client never sends a price.
+  - The delivery address is resolved from the saved `Address` (must belong to the user and have
+    verified coordinates), never from a client-sent coordinate.
+- **200 response (`data` = the quote, from `pricingOrchestrator.buildQuote`):**
+  ```jsonc
+  {
+    "success": true,
+    "data": {
+      "serviceable": true,
+      "decision": "PROFITABLE | REPRICING_REQUIRED | NOT_ECONOMICALLY_SERVICEABLE",
+      "reason": "...",
+      "restaurantId": "...",
+      "pricingVersion": "...",
+      "selfDeliveryAvailable": false,
+      "distance": { "restaurantToCustomerKm": 3.2, "riderToRestaurantKm": 1.1,
+                    "repositioningKm": 0, "totalTripKm": 4.3, "bandIndex": 1, "band": {...},
+                    "sources": {...}, "degraded": false },
+      "bill": {
+        "baseFoodSubtotal": 200, "foodUplift": 20, "customerFoodSubtotal": 220,
+        "discount": 20, "couponDiscount": 20, "autoDiscount": 0, "foodPayable": 200,
+        "deliveryFee": 25, "baseDeliveryFee": 25, "deliverySubsidy": 0,
+        "smallOrderFee": 0, "codFee": 0, "total": 225, "grandTotal": 225
+      },
+      "freeDelivery": { "available": true, "enabled": true, "threshold": 299,
+                        "baseThreshold": 299, "raised": false, "eligibleSubtotal": 220,
+                        "amountRemaining": 79, "unlocked": false, "reachedThreshold": false,
+                        "subsidised": 0, "deliveryFee": 25, "effectiveDeliveryFee": 25,
+                        "reason": "below_threshold" },
+      "discount": { "enabled": true, "maxTheoretical": 40, "recommended": 20, "reason": "..." },
+      "contribution": { "projected": 42, "required": 30, "shortfall": 0, "meetsTarget": true,
+                        "promotionFundingSource": "none", ... },
+      "riderPayout": { "guaranteedTotal": 38, ... },
+      "paise": { "customerTotalPaise": 22500, "baseSubtotalPaise": 20000, ... },
+      "paymentMethod": "upi", "isCod": false, "isFirstOrder": true,
+      "quoteIssuedAt": "ISO", "quoteExpiresAt": "ISO",
+      "quoteId": "q_<uuid>"
+    }
+  }
+  ```
+- **Errors:**
+  - `400` — invalid restaurantId / no items / no saved address with coordinates / item not in restaurant.
+  - `404` — restaurant not found/unavailable.
+  - `409` — **not serviceable**: `{ success:false, code:"NOT_ECONOMICALLY_SERVICEABLE"|"out_of_delivery_radius"|"route_unavailable", message, data:<quote> }`
+    (see `pricingController.quote`, `pricingOrchestrator` rejection branches).
+  - `429` — rate limited.
+- **Note:** `quoteId` is stamped only when `serviceable !== false` (`quoteService.createQuote`).
+
+### A2. `GET /pricing/restaurant-cards` — `controllers/pricingController.js`
+- **Auth:** `protect`. **Rate limit:** 120/min.
+- **Query:** `addressId` (optional MongoId), `restaurantIds` (comma list, ≤30), `eligibleSubtotal` (number, default 0).
+- **Response (`data`):**
+  ```jsonc
+  { "pricingVersion": "...", "cards": [ {
+      "restaurantId": "...", "pricingVersion": "...", "serviceable": true,
+      "distanceKm": 3.2, "distanceSource": "...", "distanceDegraded": false,
+      "freeDelivery": { "available": true, "threshold": 299, "baseThreshold": 299,
+                        "eligibleSubtotal": 220, "amountRemaining": 79, "unlocked": false,
+                        "firstOrderFreeDelivery": false, "reason": "..." },
+      "deliveryFee": 25, "effectiveDeliveryFee": 25, "subsidised": 0
+  } ] }
+  ```
+  Non-serviceable card: `{ restaurantId, pricingVersion, serviceable:false, distanceKm, reason:"out_of_radius"|"route_unavailable", effectiveRadiusKm? }`.
+- **400** when `addressId` resolves to no verified coords, or no valid ids.
+
+### A3. `GET /pricing/config` — `controllers/pricingController.js`
+- **Auth:** `protect`. Returns the **customer-safe** pricing config subset:
+  `pricingVersion, pricingEngineEnabled, foodPriceUpliftPercent, deliveryFeeBands, maxDeliveryDistanceKm,
+  freeDeliveryEnabled, freeDeliveryThreshold, firstOrderFreeDelivery*, smallOrderFee*, codHandlingFee*`.
+- **Use:** to label fees and (optionally) render thresholds — **display only**, never to compute a price.
+
+### Pricing engine internals (source of the numbers above)
+`services/pricing/*`: `pricingOrchestrator.js` (buildQuote, buildRestaurantCardPricing),
+`quoteService.js` (quoteId, isExpired, verifyQuote, persistSnapshot), `money.js` (integer paise;
+`fromPaise` for the API boundary), `freeDeliveryThresholdEngine.js`, `deliveryFeeEngine.js`,
+`codFeeEngine.js`, `smallOrderFeeEngine.js`, `discountOptimizer.js`, `profitabilityEngine.js`,
+`routeService.js`, `checkoutIntegration.js`.
+
+---
+
+## B. Restaurant listing / ranking
+
+### B1. `GET /restaurants` — `routes/restaurantRoutes.js`, `controllers/restaurantController.js`
+- **Auth:** public. **Query:** `veg, category, search, sort=recommended|rating|time|distance, page, limit(≤100), lat, lng`.
+- **Ordering (backend, authoritative):** default `recommended` sort key order
+  `__isOpen(-1), homeOrder(1), pinned(-1), isFeatured(-1), rankScore(-1), displayPriority(-1), rating(-1), createdAt(-1)`.
+  Online-first is the leading key for **every** sort. (See `restaurantController.getRestaurants`.)
+- **Per-restaurant fields returned:** the `CUSTOMER_LIST_PROJECTION` fields **plus**
+  `rankPosition, online, orderable, performanceScore, featured, pinned, sponsored, sponsoredLabel,
+  serviceable, distanceKm, availability (with .isOpen/.status/.closedReason), operational, isOpen`.
+  `sponsoredLabel` defaults to `"Sponsored"`.
+- **`withServiceability`** adds `distanceKm` (backend haversine) and `serviceable` when `lat`/`lng` given,
+  else `distanceKm:null, serviceable:null`.
+
+### B2. `GET /restaurants/:id` — `controllers/restaurantController.js`
+- **Auth:** public. Adds `availabilityStatus` (class), `orderable`, `performanceScore`,
+  `availabilityInfo` (from `classifyRestaurantAvailability`) on top of the restaurant view.
+
+### B3. `GET /restaurants/:id/menu` — `controllers/restaurantController.js`
+- **Auth:** public. Returns menu groups/items (Swiggy-style formatter). Unchanged contract.
+
+### B4. `GET /restaurants/search` — `controllers/restaurantController.js`
+- **Auth:** public. **Query:** `q` (2..80), `scope=home|under99|restaurant`, `restaurantId` (for scope=restaurant).
+- **Response:** `{ success, scope, query, count, data: { menuItems: [ { id, restaurantId, name, price, ...,
+  restaurant: { id, name, rating, deliveryTime, cuisine, isOpen, availability, operational } } ] } }`.
+  **Dish-first** — restaurant objects are not returned as top-level results. Only items whose
+  restaurant is currently open are returned.
+
+### B5. `GET /restaurants/under99` and `GET /restaurants/categories` — same controller.
+- `categories` returns `{ success, data: [category,...] }`.
+
+### Availability classes — `services/restaurantAvailability.js`
+`orderable | busy | temporarily_closed | closed_today | outside_hours | suspended | unapproved | inactive`.
+- `orderable`/`busy` ⇒ can accept orders. `visible=false` for `inactive|unapproved|suspended`
+  (never customer-listed). Others are visible-but-offline.
+- Labels: `temporarily_closed`→"Temporarily closed", `closed_today`→"Closed today",
+  `outside_hours`→"Outside opening hours", `suspended`→"Suspended by Eatswada", etc.
+- Ranking service: `services/restaurantRankingService.js` (`rankRestaurants`, `withServiceability`,
+  `getRankingConfig`). Config: `models/RankingConfig.js` (`sponsoredEnabled`, `sponsoredScoreBoost`,
+  `maxSponsoredSlots`).
+
+---
+
+## C. Menu views & customer activity analytics
+
+### C1. `POST /analytics/visit` — `routes/analyticsRoutes.js`, `controllers/analyticsController.js`
+- **Auth:** `optionalAuth` (works for guests **and** logged-in). **Rate limit:** 60/min keyed by user or IP.
+- **Allowed client event types (whitelist):**
+  - platform: `site_visit`, `search`
+  - restaurant: `restaurant_view`, `menu_view`
+  - item: `item_view`, `add_to_cart`, `remove_from_cart`, `checkout_initiated`
+  - **Outcome events (`order_completed`, `order_cancelled`, `refund`) are REJECTED** — server-only.
+- **Body:**
+  ```json
+  { "eventType": "menu_view", "restaurantId": "<24hex>", "menuItemId": "<24hex|null>",
+    "sessionId": "opaque-string", "eventKey": "uuid", "platform": "web",
+    "referrer": "...", "source": "web" }
+  ```
+- **Validation:** `restaurantId` must be a valid MongoId **and** the restaurant must exist and be
+  customer-visible; `menuItemId` must belong to that restaurant.
+- **Response:** `202 { success:true, data:{ recorded: bool, ... } }` (fire-and-forget).
+- **Dedupe:** server builds `dedupeKey` over a **configurable time bucket**
+  (`ANALYTICS_VIEW_DEDUPE_WINDOW_MS`, default 30 min). If the client sends `eventKey`, the key is
+  `eventType:key:<eventKey>` → a retried beacon can never double-count. (`services/analyticsService.js`
+  `dedupeKeyFor`, `dedupeWindowMs`.)
+- **Privacy:** no raw IP persisted; `visitorKey`/`sessionKey` are salted SHA-256 hashes; bot UAs filtered.
+- **Event model:** `models/AnalyticsEvent.js` (`EVENT_TYPES`, `dedupeKey` unique, `day` Asia/Kolkata bucket).
+
+---
+
+## D. Order creation & payment
+
+### D1. `POST /orders` — `routes/orderRoutes.js`, `controllers/orderController.js`
+- **Auth:** `protect`. **Rate limit:** 10 / 10 min per account.
+- **Idempotency:** client may send `Idempotency-Key` header **or** `body.idempotencyKey`
+  (`services/checkoutIdempotencyService.js` `resolveCheckoutKey`). Sequential replay returns the same
+  orders with `200 { replay:true }`; concurrent double-tap is closed by an atomic `IdempotencyKey` lock.
+- **Accepted body fields (validated):** `items[]` (1..50, each `menuItem|menuId|id|_id` + `quantity` 1..99),
+  `addressId`, `deliveryAddress`, `paymentMethod` (`upi|cod`), `tipAmount` (0..500),
+  `restaurantNote`, `restaurantNotes`, `globalNote`, `deliveryInstructions`, `couponCode`,
+  `sendCutlery`, `idempotencyKey`.
+- **NOT accepted:** `quoteId` — **the backend ignores it entirely** (see BACKEND_GAPS.md B1).
+- **Money is fully recomputed server-side** (`buildRestaurantPricing` → engine or legacy bill). Client
+  `subtotal`/`deliveryFee`/`total` are ignored.
+- **Success `201`** (single restaurant):
+  ```jsonc
+  { "success": true, "replay": false, "checkoutGroupId": "...",
+    "data": { "_id":"...", "orderNumber":"...", "total":225, "grandTotal":225,
+              "bill": { "itemSubtotal":200, "deliveryFee":25, "baseDeliveryFee":25,
+                        "isFreeDeliveryApplied":false, "smallCartFee":0, "discountAmount":20,
+                        "taxAmount":0, "tipAmount":0, "grandTotal":225,
+                        "baseFoodSubtotal":200, "foodUplift":20, "customerFoodSubtotal":220,
+                        "deliverySubsidy":0, "codFee":0, "autoDiscount":0, "couponDiscount":20 },
+              "financialSnapshot": { "snapshotId":"...", "decision":"PROFITABLE",
+                        "expectedContribution":42, "minimumRequiredContribution":30,
+                        "riderGuaranteedPayout":38, "foodPriceUplift":20,
+                        "quoteIssuedAt":"ISO", "quoteExpiresAt":"ISO", "pricingRuleVersion":"..." },
+              "paymentStatus":"pending", "paymentMethod":"upi", ... },
+    "deliveryOtp": "1234",
+    "payment": { "provider":"razorpay", "keyId":"rzp_...", "orderId":"order_...", "amount":22500, "currency":"INR" } }
+  ```
+  Multi-restaurant adds `multiple:true, count, orders[], deliveryOtps{}`.
+- **Error codes returned (real, from the controller):**
+  - `503 { code:"PLATFORM_MAINTENANCE" }` — maintenance.
+  - `403 { code:"ACCOUNT_FROZEN" }` — frozen account.
+  - `409 { code:"NOT_ECONOMICALLY_SERVICEABLE", selfDeliveryAvailable }` — engine rejected.
+  - `409 { code:"COD_ADVANCE_REQUIRED" }` — COD advance not yet paid (status-change path).
+  - Plus plain `400/403/404/409` messages for closed restaurant, out of radius, min order, out of stock,
+    coupon problems, COD/UPI disabled, etc. (no `code` field on those).
+  - **There are NO quote-specific error codes** (no `QUOTE_EXPIRED`/`PRICE_CHANGED`), because the
+    backend never verifies a quote here.
+
+### D2. `GET /orders` (history) and `GET /orders/:id` — `controllers/orderController.js`
+- **Auth:** `protect` (own orders only). Return `withLiveDisplayData(order)` + rider live position.
+  Includes `bill` (itemized), `financialSnapshot`, `paymentStatus`, `partialCod*`, `refund`.
+- **Order status change / cancel / review:** `PUT /orders/:id/cancel`, `PUT /orders/:id/rate`,
+  `POST|PUT /orders/:id/review`, `POST /orders/reviews/:reviewId/report`.
+
+### D3. Payments — `routes/paymentRoutes.js`, `controllers/paymentController.js`
+- `POST /payments/verify` — body `{ orderId, razorpayPaymentId, razorpayOrderId, razorpaySignature }`.
+  `409` = capture race (reconcile), explicit failure only on a server failure verdict.
+- `POST /payments/retry` — body `{ orderId }` (re-creates a Razorpay order).
+- `GET /payments/:id/status` — authoritative status for reconciliation.
+- **Razorpay key/amount come from the backend response** (`payment.keyId`, `payment.amount`) — the
+  client must never hold the key.
+
+### D4. Cart (server cart) — `routes/cartRoutes.js` (all `protect`)
+- `GET /cart`, `POST /cart/add`, `PUT /cart/update`, `DELETE /cart/item/:menuItemId`,
+  `DELETE /cart/clear`, `PATCH /cart/address`, `PATCH /cart/payment`.
+- The customer site currently uses a **local** cart; the server cart is optional and not required by
+  this task.
+
+### D5. Coupons — `routes/couponRoutes.js`
+- `POST /coupons/validate` (`protect`) — validates a code. Returns the backend's decision only; the
+  client shows no amount of its own.
+
+### D6. Addresses — `routes/userRoutes.js`
+- `GET/POST /users/addresses`, `PUT/DELETE /users/addresses/:id`, `PATCH /users/addresses/:id/default`.
+- Body fields: `tag, house, area, landmark, city, pincode, coordinates|[lng,lat]|latitude+longitude, isDefault`.
+
+---
+
+## E. Contract verification asked for in the task
+
+> **Does `POST /orders` now read and verify `quoteId`?**
+
+**No.** `grep -rn "quoteId"` across the backend returns exactly **one** hit:
+`services/pricing/quoteService.js:35` (where the id is *created*). `POST /orders`
+(`controllers/orderController.js` `createOrder`) never destructures or reads `quoteId`, and
+`validateMiddleware`/`createOrderValidation` do not validate it. A stale or forged quoteId has no
+effect on the price charged.
+
+> **What error codes does it return for expired or mismatched quotes?**
+
+**None.** There is no quote-expiry or price-change error path in order creation. `quoteService.isExpired`
+and `verifyQuote` exist but are **not called** from the order or payment flow. The only related code is
+the engine's `409 NOT_ECONOMICALLY_SERVICEABLE`.
+
+Both facts are logged as **release blockers** in `BACKEND_GAPS.md`.
