+# Backend gaps & release blockers
+
+Backend: `kignas/Eatswada-` @ `2139abb`. **Nothing in the backend is modified by this task** — this
+file records mismatches between what the task asks the frontend to do and what the backend actually
+supports, so they can be fixed on the backend side.
+
+---
+
+## B1 — RELEASE BLOCKER: `POST /orders` does not read or verify `quoteId`
+
+**Evidence.** `grep -rn "quoteId" --include=*.js` over the whole backend returns a single line:
+`services/pricing/quoteService.js:35` (`quote.quoteId = 'q_' + crypto.randomUUID()`). The quote id is
+produced but never consumed. `controllers/orderController.js#createOrder` does not destructure
+`quoteId`, and `createOrderValidation` in `routes/orderRoutes.js` does not validate it.
+
+**Consequence.** The customer can be shown a quote at price A, then the order is created from a fresh
+server-side re-price at price B, with no verification that the customer saw B. There is also no
+protection against a forged/stale quoteId. The task's Phase-3 requirement — "Use the backend's actual
+quote-error codes … instead of a generic error" — **cannot be met**, because no such codes exist.
+
+**What the frontend does anyway (as instructed).** It keeps sending `quoteId` on `POST /orders` and on
+`/payments/*`, plus an idempotency key per attempt. If/when the backend verifies it, the frontend is
+already correct.
+
+**What the backend must add (proposal, not implemented here).**
+1. Accept and validate `quoteId` on `POST /orders`.
+2. Re-verify the quote (`quoteService.verifyQuote`) against a freshly rebuilt quote.
+3. Return distinct error codes, e.g. `409 QUOTE_EXPIRED`, `409 QUOTE_PRICE_CHANGED` (with the new
+   totals), `409 QUOTE_MISMATCH`. The frontend already has handling hooks ready for these codes
+   (`js/pricing-client.js` + `js/cart-page.js` re-quote path) and will show the revised bill.
+
+---
+
+## B2 — No dedicated "self-delivery available" flag on the order-rejection path for the frontend
+
+The engine rejection (`409 NOT_ECONOMICALLY_SERVICEABLE`) includes `selfDeliveryAvailable: true|false`
+(see `orderController.js` ~line 693). The **quote** endpoint also returns `selfDeliveryAvailable`
+(`pricingOrchestrator.buildQuote`). This is enough for the frontend to offer self-delivery. **No gap**,
+recorded only for completeness.
+
+---
+
+## B3 — Free-delivery "unlocked" semantics differ between card and quote
+
+- Card (`buildRestaurantCardPricing`) returns `freeDelivery.unlocked = freeDelivery.unlocked || firstOrderEligible`.
+- Quote (`buildQuote`) returns `freeDelivery.unlocked = deliverySubsidyPaise > 0` (only when the
+  subsidy was actually granted after the contribution test).
+
+**Consequence.** A card can show "Free delivery unlocked" while checkout still charges a fee if the
+contribution test fails at checkout time (different basket / COD). The frontend renders exactly what
+each endpoint says (per the rules) and does **not** reconcile them client-side, but the two can
+visibly disagree. **Recommend** the card endpoint gate `unlocked` on the same contribution test, or the
+frontend should treat the quote as the only authority once the cart page is open (it does).
+
+---
+
+## B4 — `GET /restaurants/search` is dish-first (no top-level restaurant results)
+
+The homepage search returns `data.menuItems[]` only; restaurant objects appear nested inside each item.
+The legacy overlay already handles this shape. No change required, but the task's "search results must
+use backend order/values" is satisfied by rendering `menuItems` in the returned order. **No gap.**
+
+---
+
+## B5 — Analytics: no server-side `menu_view` auto-emit
+
+The frontend must POST `menu_view`/`item_view`/`add_to_cart`/`remove_from_cart`/`checkout_initiated`
+itself; the server only records outcome events. This matches the task. **No gap**, but the client is
+the only source of browse/funnel data, so a blocked beacon means a lost view (by design; dedupe window
+defaults to 30 min).
+
+---
+
+## B6 — `POST /analytics/visit` rate limit is 60/min per user/IP
+
+A user browsing many menus/items quickly can hit `429`. The frontend swallows analytics errors (per
+rules) so this never breaks the UI, but it means high-frequency events may be dropped. **Accepted.**
+
+---
+
+## B7 — Idempotency key header is `Idempotency-Key` (also accepted in body)
+
+Confirmed in `services/checkoutIdempotencyService.js#resolveCheckoutKey`. The legacy cart already sends
+the header. **No gap.**
+
+---
+
+## B8 — `quoteId` has no TTL enforcement server-side
+
+`quoteService.isExpired` exists but is unused, so an expired quote id (if the backend later starts
+verifying it) would need the expiry check wired in. The frontend still runs its own countdown from
+`quoteExpiresAt` and auto re-quotes. **Rolled into B1.**
+
+---
+
+## B9 — No endpoint to fetch a single saved quote by id
+
+There is no `GET /pricing/quote/:id`. The frontend re-quotes by re-POSTing the current cart instead.
+**Accepted** (re-quote is the correct behaviour on expiry anyway).
